# COVENANT_FLOW.vsm — Governance of covenant.vsm Integrity

This document formalizes the system that keeps covenant.vsm trustworthy.
It is not a policy document — that is covenant.vsm itself.
This is the operational system that governs how covenant.vsm moves,
is signed, deployed, and verified.

The system is defined using VSF/VSM notation (Beer 1972):
S1 Operations | S2 Coordination | S3 Control | S4 Intelligence | S5 Policy


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S5 — POLICY (the covenant text itself)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  File:     covenant.vsm  (this repository)
  Content:  A0 / A0.1 axioms, signatories, watermark convention
  Rule:     S5 cannot be edited without triggering S3 release gate.
            A change to A0 or A0.1 requires re-signing by all
            active signatories (status: VERIFIED).

  Self-reference:
    The document whose integrity this system protects is itself
    the policy that authorizes this system.
    Resolution: S5 is frozen per version. A new version is a new S5.


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S4 — INTELLIGENCE (amendment channel)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Who proposes:   any signatory or community contributor (GitHub issue / PR)
  Who decides:    rmw3 (founding author) — single-loop approval
  Threshold:      changes to A0 / A0.1 require explicit re-signing
                  by all nodes with status: VERIFIED
  Channel:        git PR on vsf-sandbox → discussion → S3 release gate
  Constraint:     D4 (VSF): double-loop corrections require human approval


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S3 — CONTROL (release gate)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Trigger:        any edit to covenant.vsm, regardless of scope
  Gate owner:     rmw3 (sole authorized releaser at this governance stage)

  Release protocol (signing ceremony):

    Step 1 — FREEZE
      Edit covenant.vsm in vsf-sandbox (S1.1).
      No changes after this point until the ceremony completes.

    Step 2 — COMPUTE
      sha256sum covenant.vsm
      Record the hash. This is the canonical hash for this version.

    Step 3 — EMBED
      Add to covenant.vsm footer:
        Covenant SHA-256 (v<N>): <hash>
        Note: hash is of content EXCLUDING this line and below.
      Add to LICENSE footer:
        Covenant SHA-256: <hash>
      Add to vsf-infra/bastion/LICENSE.es footer:
        SHA-256 del Convenio: <hash>

    Step 4 — COMMIT
      git add covenant.vsm LICENSE README.md
      git commit -m "covenant: v<N> signed — SHA-256 embedded"
      git push origin main
      (vsf-infra: git add bastion/LICENSE.es + commit + push)

    Step 5 — DEPLOY
      scp vsf-sandbox/covenant.vsm n01:/home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/covenant.vsm
      scp vsf-sandbox/LICENSE n01:/home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/LICENSE
      ssh n01-vsf "sudo systemctl restart vsf-bastion"

    Step 6 — VERIFY
      curl -s https://vsf.u2738.org/covenant | grep "SHA-256"
      → must match the committed hash

  Version bump rule:
    Any content change → new version number (0.3 → 0.4 → 1.0)
    Hash-only embed (no content change) → same version, append "(signed)"
    v1.0 = first fully signed public release


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S2 — COORDINATION (sync rules — prevents divergence)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Rule 1 — Single Write Origin
    vsf-sandbox/covenant.vsm is the ONLY writable origin.
    n01 is read-only from covenant.vsm's perspective:
    it receives files via deploy, never via direct edit.

  Rule 2 — No Direct Edit on n01
    Never: ssh n01 "nano /home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/covenant.vsm"
    Always: edit locally → commit → scp deploy

  Rule 3 — LICENSE.es lives in vsf-infra
    vsf-infra/bastion/LICENSE.es contains the Spanish hash anchor.
    It must be updated in the same commit as the signing ceremony.

  Rule 4 — Hash anchors are synchronized
    After any signing ceremony, all three hash anchors must agree:
      vsf-sandbox/LICENSE          → Covenant SHA-256: <hash>
      vsf-infra/bastion/LICENSE.es → SHA-256 del Convenio: <hash>
      covenant.vsm footer          → Covenant SHA-256 (vN): <hash>

  Divergence detection:
    sha256sum /home/rmw3/vsf-sandbox/covenant.vsm
    ssh n01 "sha256sum /home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/covenant.vsm"
    → both must match


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
S1 — OPERATIONS (physical file instances)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  S1.1 — canonical origin (read-write)
    Path:   /home/rmw3/vsf-sandbox/covenant.vsm
    Repo:   github.com/rm-w3kufe/vsf-sandbox  (public)
    Access: rmw3 local + git push
    Role:   source of truth — all other copies derive from here

  S1.2 — live deployed instance (read-only from governance perspective)
    Path:   n01:/home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/covenant.vsm
    Served: https://vsf.u2738.org/covenant
    Access: scp from rmw3 only (no direct edit)
    Role:   public-facing endpoint — what users and verifiers see

  S1.3 — hash anchor (English)
    Path:   /home/rmw3/vsf-sandbox/LICENSE
    Also:   n01:/home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/LICENSE
    Field:  "Covenant SHA-256: <hash>"
    Role:   public anchor — anyone can verify covenant.vsm integrity

  S1.4 — hash anchor (Spanish)
    Path:   /home/rmw3/vsf-infra/bastion/LICENSE.es
    Also:   n01:/home/rmw3/vsf-bastion/LICENSE.es
    Field:  "SHA-256 del Convenio: <hash>"
    Role:   Spanish-language anchor — same integrity guarantee

  S1.5 — /covenant endpoint (derived)
    URL:    https://vsf.u2738.org/covenant
    Source: FastAPI serves covenant.vsm content + hash from LICENSE
    Role:   human-readable verification page (DEBT-02 when hash is live)


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
VERIFICATION PROCEDURE (for third parties)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  1. Download covenant.vsm from:
       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rm-w3kufe/vsf-sandbox/main/covenant.vsm

  2. Strip the "Covenant SHA-256" footer line and everything below it.
     Canonical content ends at the last non-hash line before the footer.

  3. Compute: sha256sum covenant.vsm (stripped)

  4. Compare with the hash published in:
       LICENSE (same repo)
       https://vsf.u2738.org/covenant (live endpoint)

  5. Match → document has not been tampered with since signing.
     Mismatch → flag as integrity failure; contact rmw3kufe@proton.me


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
CANONICAL FLOW DIAGRAM
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  PROPOSE ──► S4 (amendment channel)
                │  PR / discussion
                ▼
  APPROVE ──► S3 (release gate — rmw3)
                │  signing ceremony
                ▼
  COMMIT  ──► S1.1 (vsf-sandbox/covenant.vsm)  ← single write origin
                │  git push + scp deploy
                ▼
  DEPLOY  ──► S1.2 (n01/covenant.vsm)           ← live endpoint
                │  served at /covenant
                ▼
  VERIFY  ──► anyone: sha256sum → compare LICENSE → pass/fail

  S2 enforces: S1.2 never receives writes except from S1.1 via S3


